add('spacebok-design','SpaceBok: A Dynamic Legged Robot for Space Exploration','2019',g,'Model-based · elastic hardware','https://doi.org/10.1109/ICRA.2019.8794136','A purpose-built quadruped uses leg geometry and parallel elasticity for powerful hopping.','The primary paper reports physical walking, trotting and pronking, with single jumps up to 1.05 m. Lunar-pronking predictions are simulated.','Earth jumping does not establish operation in lunar dust, vacuum or thermal extremes. ETH describes the platform as not space-graded.','Hardware + low-gravity simulation','Earth-based physical robot; simulated lunar locomotion.','Elastic mechanism and model-based control; order not audited.','Hardware/control co-design.','https://www.esa.int/Enabling_Support/Space_Engineering_Technology/Jumping_space_robot_flies_like_a_spacecraft',verification='ETH-hosted paper and ETH platform description checked.',environment='Extraterrestrial motivation; hardware tests on Earth.',sources=[{'url':'https://www.research-collection.ethz.ch/bitstream/handle/20.500.11850/384203/ICRA19_0651_FI.pdf?isAllowed=y&sequence=1','label':'ETH paper'},{'url':'https://rsl.ethz.ch/robots-media/spacebok.html/','label':'ETH platform'}])
add('spacehopper','SpaceHopper: A Small-Scale Legged Robot for Exploring Low-Gravity Celestial Bodies','2024',g,'RL · limb-based attitude control','https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.02831','A three-legged robot explores how moving limbs can orient the body during long low-gravity flights. This is related work, not a quadruped.','Physical tests use a rotational gimbal and counterweight setup. Six-metre commanded jumps are reported in simulated Ceres gravity (0.029 g).','The simulated distance is not a hardware jump record. Gimbal and counterweight tests do not establish autonomous flight and landing on an asteroid.','Hardware testbed + simulation','5.2 kg three-legged robot; Earth gimbal / counterweight rigs.','Articulated robot simulation for RL.','Learned leg-based aerial reorientation.',environment='Asteroid / moon target; simulation and Earth-based tests.')
g='Bipedal connections & foundations'
add('deepmimic','DeepMimic: Example-Guided Deep Reinforcement Learning of Physics-Based Character Skills','2018',g,'RL · motion imitation','https://doi.org/10.1145/3197517.3201311','A shared imitation-plus-task formulation learns diverse motions in simulated characters.','Demonstrates acrobatics, locomotion and recovery across simulated human, Atlas, dinosaur and dragon characters.','A simulated Atlas character is not a physical Atlas experiment. This provides methodological ancestry, not evidence of quadruped-to-biped hardware policy transfer.','Simulation only','Physics-based character animation; no physical hardware demonstration.','Full articulated character simulation.','Reference-motion tracking through RL.','https://xbpeng.github.io/projects/DeepMimic/index.html',verification='Author project and primary paper checked.',sources=[{'url':'https://xbpeng.github.io/projects/DeepMimic/index.html','label':'Author project'}])
add('animal-imitation','Learning Agile Robotic Locomotion Skills by Imitating Animals','2020',g,'RL · imitation · sim-to-real','https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.00784','Retargets animal motion references to learn robot skills, extending motion-imitation ideas to physical quadrupeds.','Reports physical quadruped locomotion, dynamic hops and turns from reference-guided learning.','Reference availability, retargeting and simulator mismatch matter. It does not show that a humanoid controller can be copied unchanged onto a quadruped.','Hardware','Physical quadruped demonstrations after simulation training.','Articulated simulation; learned policy at deployment.','Motion retargeting + imitation RL + sim-to-real.','https://xbpeng.github.io/projects/Robotic_Imitation/index.html',verification='Primary abstract and author project checked.')
add('asap','ASAP: Aligning Simulation and Real-World Physics for Learning Agile Humanoid Whole-Body Skills','2025',g,'RL · imitation · residual sim alignment','https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01143','Uses real robot rollouts to learn an action correction inside the simulator, then fine-tunes the motion policy.','Unitree G1 hardware demonstrates agile human-like skills; author examples include forward and sideways jumps and a jump with rotation.','Requires real-world data collection. This is a humanoid method with related ingredients, not demonstrated quadruped-to-humanoid acrobatic transfer.','Hardware','Unitree G1 physical demonstrations and simulator-transfer experiments.','Articulated simulation corrected by learned delta actions.','Two-stage motion imitation and sim-to-real fine-tuning.','https://agile.human2humanoid.com/',verification='Author project and primary abstract checked; RSS 2025.')
add('beyondmimic','BeyondMimic: From Motion Tracking to Versatile Humanoid Control via Guided Diffusion','2025',g,'RL tracking · guided diffusion','https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.08241','First learn dynamic motion tracking, then distill selected motion policies into a guided diffusion policy.','The tracking pipeline demonstrates jumping spins and cartwheels; diffusion demonstrations include waypoint following, teleoperation and obstacle avoidance.','Do not attribute every acrobatic tracker result to the unified diffusion controller. The project uses motion capture for some navigation / state-estimation demonstrations.','Hardware','Humanoid physical demonstrations; motion-capture-assisted downstream tests.','Articulated training simulation; distilled generative policy.','RL motion tracking + diffusion distillation + test-time guidance.','https://beyondmimic.github.io/',verification='Author project and 2025 preprint abstract checked; results separated by pipeline stage.')
